{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED for notes/2026-08-26-jsonata-ddl-application-interface.md at exact head 2511990b01d852db12700c7ee5aa21c5da292efb (implementation-report artifact 264cbdd6, request #11830, governing ratified decision #6).\n\nArchitecture: the note touches layers 4 (host binding), 5 (application profile and interpreter) and 6 (projections and queries) of docs/reference/architecture.md and restates layer 2 faithfully. It claims no contract change and ships none, so no page update is owed at this head. Tighten lines 118-119 so \"part of the bound application identity\" cannot be read as widening the gitseq/app-binding@0 record.\n\nSecurity - three unresolved defects, all in what the interface commits to:\n1. Determinism hole (decisive). Read purity is specified (lines 133-137) but the JSONata expression itself is unconstrained: standard builtins $now, $random and $eval let a fold observe a clock or randomness through the language rather than through a read. One sentence pinning a deterministic, total function subset closes it.\n2. Unknown event kinds (decisive). Contract step 1 (line 107) presupposes a CREATE EVENT declaration exists; the note never says that kinds without a declaration or fold binding remain opaque and untranslated, which governing decision #6 (\"unknown kinds remain opaque\") requires of this interface.\n3. Bounds and helper confinement. Only read cardinality is bounded (line 135); evaluation time, memory, recursion depth and row-change volume have no declarable bounds, and native helper functions (lines 158-160) carry the right purity contract but impose no stated obligation on the follow-up design to confine them.\n\nSound and worth keeping: typed validation before atomic apply (105-112), the separation of business rejection from execution failure with fail-stop semantics (123-127), position-pinned versioned reads (139-141), and the disposable-derived-state claim grounded in verified events plus the bound application (150-153).\n\nSimplification (non-blocking): facts may be cut from the minimal interface or moved to Small extensions; helper functions could move wholesale into the follow-up design until confinement is answered; drop direction-setting prose such as line 157; pick one term for the platform actor. Plain English passes overall.\n\nEvidence basis: full read of the note at this exact head via git show (single .md file added, confirmed by git show --stat); no Go code changed, so build/test scope does not apply to this head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:264cbdd6dc30aad217eaf6c5af2ec14eb39eadd8","head":"2511990b01d852db12700c7ee5aa21c5da292efb","verdict":"changes-requested"}}